4. THE SINGLE-MASS AND SINGLE-LENGTH CONSTRUCTIONS -- what a_0 can say about one system
==============================================================================================================================
  With one mass M the complete list is r_M = sqrt(GM/a_0), v_M = (G M a_0)^(1/4), t_M = r_M/v_M,
  j_M = (GM)^(3/4) a_0^(-1/4), E_M = sqrt(G a_0) M^(3/2), rho_M = a_0^(3/2)/(G^(3/2) M^(1/2)), and the
  MASS-FREE Sigma_M = a_0/(2 pi G).  Every one of these is either credited (Milgrom) or already in the ledger:
    r_M   -> items 3 (dead), 24, 95, 108 (refuted)      v_M -> the BTFR                Sigma_M -> items 5 (keeper), 6 (dead), 122
    j_M   -> item 26 (naive 3/4 excluded at 7.4 sigma)   rho_M -> items 110, 92        E_M -> restatement of the BTFR

  canonical:  the three a_0-natural scales that need c as well
     M_* = c^4/(G a_0) = 1.2930e+54 kg = 6.5011e+23 Msun     (the mass whose MOND radius is its own Schwarzschild radius x 4)
     L_* = c^2/a_0     = 9.6021e+26 m  =  31118.24 Mpc      = Z c/H_Lambda
     T_* = c/a_0       = 3.2029e+18 s  =    101.50 Gyr      = Z/H_Lambda
     BTFR in a_0-natural form (an exact restatement):  v_flat/c = (M_b/M_*)^(1/4);  v_flat = 200 km/s <-> M_b = 1.288e+11 Msun

  alt:  the three a_0-natural scales that need c as well
     M_* = c^4/(G a_0) = 1.0710e+54 kg = 5.3849e+23 Msun     (the mass whose MOND radius is its own Schwarzschild radius x 4)
     L_* = c^2/a_0     = 7.9536e+26 m  =  25775.82 Mpc      = Z c/H_Lambda
     T_* = c/a_0       = 2.6530e+18 s  =     84.07 Gyr      = Z/H_Lambda
     BTFR in a_0-natural form (an exact restatement):  v_flat/c = (M_b/M_*)^(1/4);  v_flat = 200 km/s <-> M_b = 1.067e+11 Msun

  Anchor for M_*: the matter inside the Hubble volume is 2.911e+52 kg = 1.464e+22 Msun;
  M_*/M_Hubble = 44.42 (canonical) / 36.79 (alt).
  FLAGGED AS NUMEROLOGY: this is the Dirac large-number coincidence in a_0 clothing.  It follows algebraically
  from a_0 ~ cH and carries no independent content; it must not be quoted as a prediction.

